WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.188 --> 00:00:15.717
The king the duke climbed aboard the raft.

2
00:00:16.578 --> 00:00:18.480
The king grabbed my collar and shook me.

3
00:00:18.500 --> 00:00:21.542
"Trying to get away from us, were you?"

4
00:00:21.562 --> 00:00:24.024
"No, Your Majesty, we weren't!

5
00:00:25.065 --> 00:00:27.987
Please let me go and I'll tell you the truth," I said.

6
00:00:29.588 --> 00:00:33.872
I quickly made up a story: "The man who was holding me felt sorry for me.

7
00:00:34.732 --> 00:00:37.033
He told me to run away or I would be hanged at once.

8
00:00:38.113 --> 00:00:40.635
I thought you two would be hanged, so Jim and I left.

9
00:00:41.515 --> 00:00:43.556
But we're both very glad to see you alive."

10
00:00:46.037 --> 00:00:49.458
Jim agreed eagerly, and both men seemed to calm down.

11
00:00:50.419 --> 00:00:52.800
They admitted they hadn't thought of trying to save me.

12
00:00:53.840 --> 00:00:56.921
They had run away, too, while everyone was looking at the gold.

13
00:00:56.941 --> 00:01:02.624
"I always thought those slaves that we sold stole the gold," said the king.

14
00:01:03.720 --> 00:01:05.861
"So who do you think put it in the coffin?"

15
00:01:07.202 --> 00:01:10.163
My heart pounded, but the king wasn't looking at me.

16
00:01:11.143 --> 00:01:13.204
He was looking angrily at the duke.

17
00:01:13.224 --> 00:01:16.525
"It certainly wasn't me, you old scoundrel!"

18
00:01:17.105 --> 00:01:17.906
exclaimed the duke.

19
00:01:17.926 --> 00:01:21.987
"I think it was you, trying to keep the gold for yourself!"

20
00:01:23.668 --> 00:01:27.350
In seconds, they were rolling around on the raft, punching each other.

21
00:01:28.170 --> 00:01:34.313
But when the duke began to choke the king, the old man gasped, "All right, I admit it.

22
00:01:35.293 --> 00:01:35.794
I did it.

23
00:01:36.574 --> 00:01:37.835
Now let me go!"

24
00:01:39.356 --> 00:01:43.319
The king crawled into the hut on the raft and began to drink whiskey.

25
00:01:44.400 --> 00:01:47.142
The duke soon joined him, and they shared the bottle.

26
00:01:48.943 --> 00:01:52.486
After a little while, they both fell asleep, snoring loudly.

27
00:01:53.086 --> 00:01:55.808
Then I finally told Jim everything that had happened.

28
00:01:56.829 --> 00:02:00.912
We were far south on the Mississippi River now and a long way from home.

29
00:02:03.052 --> 00:02:06.494
The next morning, the king and the duke decided to be friends again.

30
00:02:08.075 --> 00:02:11.517
They wanted to think up a new scam and go back to cheating people.

31
00:02:12.677 --> 00:02:18.060
At different towns along the river, they tried putting on plays and giving talks about the evils of

32
00:02:18.100 --> 00:02:18.880
drinking alcohol.

33
00:02:20.161 --> 00:02:24.023
They even tried fortune-telling, but nothing was really successful.

34
00:02:25.044 --> 00:02:26.464
Now they were running out of money.

35
00:02:28.686 --> 00:02:32.608
For the next few days, the king and the duke spent a lot of their time in the

36
00:02:32.648 --> 00:02:34.377
hut, whispering to each other.

37
00:02:35.377 --> 00:02:37.058
Jim and I felt very uneasy.

38
00:02:38.099 --> 00:02:43.582
We were afraid that they were planning something even worse than before, but we didn't know what it

39
00:02:43.662 --> 00:02:51.527
was. When we came to a shabby little place called Pikesville, the king said he would go see

40
00:02:51.587 --> 00:02:54.328
if anyone in town had heard of the Royal Nonesuch.

41
00:02:55.289 --> 00:03:00.352
If they hadn't, then he and the duke would stage it again because it always earned them lots

42
00:03:00.412 --> 00:03:00.732
of money.

43
00:03:01.812 --> 00:03:06.014
He told us that if he didn't come back before noon, it meant everything was all right.

44
00:03:07.334 --> 00:03:10.396
In that case, the duke and I should join him in Pikesville.

45
00:03:11.636 --> 00:03:13.817
The duke seemed nervous after the king left.

46
00:03:14.217 --> 00:03:17.398
He was cranky with Jim and me and impatient.

47
00:03:18.379 --> 00:03:22.520
When noon came and the king had not returned, the duke and I headed into town.

48
00:03:23.481 --> 00:03:25.462
It took us a long time to find the king.

49
00:03:27.222 --> 00:03:31.004
When we finally discovered him in a dirty little tavern, he was drunk.

50
00:03:32.268 --> 00:03:33.448
The duke was furious.

51
00:03:34.569 --> 00:03:39.590
The two men started cursing each other, and I ran out of the tavern and down to the

52
00:03:39.630 --> 00:03:45.072
riverbank. "Jim," I called, "this is our chance to get away from those scoundrels.

53
00:03:46.052 --> 00:03:47.492
Untie the rope and let's go!"

54
00:03:49.333 --> 00:03:50.733
But there was no answer.

55
00:03:51.353 --> 00:03:53.154
No one came out of the hut on the raft.

56
00:03:54.414 --> 00:03:57.135
I ran up and down the wooded shoreline screaming for Jim.

57
00:03:58.095 --> 00:03:59.896
It was no use; he was gone.

58
00:04:00.748 --> 00:04:02.609
I sat down on the bank and cried.

59
00:04:03.589 --> 00:04:06.770
When I realized that crying wouldn't help me, I stopped.

60
00:04:08.690 --> 00:04:12.071
I started down the road away from town, and I met a boy.

61
00:04:13.052 --> 00:04:17.033
I asked him if he had seen a black man, and I described Jim's clothes.

62
00:04:18.013 --> 00:04:19.834
Yes, he said, he'd seen that man.

63
00:04:20.294 --> 00:04:21.514
He was a runaway slave.

64
00:04:22.515 --> 00:04:28.048
A man named Silas Phelps had bought him from an old man for forty dollars.

65
00:04:28.088 --> 00:04:30.569
The old man had shown Silas a poster about the slave.

66
00:04:31.970 --> 00:04:35.192
It said the slave had run away from a plantation near New Orleans.

67
00:04:36.212 --> 00:04:39.393
Whoever took him back there would get a two-hundred-dollar reward.

68
00:04:40.174 --> 00:04:44.436
But the old man said he was too tired to go any farther, and that was why he

69
00:04:44.476 --> 00:04:46.216
was giving Phelps such a bargain.

70
00:04:49.478 --> 00:04:50.819
I had to sit down and think.

71
00:04:51.479 --> 00:04:53.680
I realized that the old man was the king.

72
00:04:54.600 --> 00:04:59.122
I remembered the poster that the duke had printed, describing Jim as a runaway slave.

73
00:05:00.142 --> 00:05:04.964
And now I reckoned that the king had waited for the duke and me to leave the raft,

74
00:05:05.685 --> 00:05:08.846
and then came back for Jim and used the poster to sell him.

75
00:05:10.567 --> 00:05:11.707
I felt sick at heart.

76
00:05:12.208 --> 00:05:13.168
I was only a boy.

77
00:05:13.808 --> 00:05:15.329
What could I do to save Jim?

78
00:05:16.529 --> 00:05:18.170
Maybe I had done all I could.

79
00:05:19.191 --> 00:05:22.292
Maybe I should write to Miss Watson and tell her where Jim was.

80
00:05:23.364 --> 00:05:25.306
After all, he was her property.

81
00:05:25.967 --> 00:05:26.687
That was the law.

82
00:05:27.668 --> 00:05:32.272
I told myself that if Jim had to be a slave again, he would be happier back home

83
00:05:32.312 --> 00:05:33.093
with people he knew.

84
00:05:33.113 --> 00:05:35.695
Here, he didn't know anyone.

85
00:05:37.216 --> 00:05:40.039
But then I remembered how Jim had called me his friend.

86
00:05:40.960 --> 00:05:44.543
I thought about how much he wanted to be free and see his family again.

87
00:05:45.403 --> 00:05:48.046
And I decided that I wouldn't write to Miss Watson.

88
00:05:48.926 --> 00:05:52.914
Even if the law said it was wrong, I was going to find a way to help free

89
00:05:52.934 --> 00:05:53.074
him.
